{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The fear of</b> — negative commandments." "And he said: <b>pure</b> — for pure means that it will not be sullied by negative commandments." "<b>Standing forever</b> — that it is not possible that HaShem will permit the forbidden. And corresponding to the sun he said pure, because there are times when the sun is overcast, even though its body is pure; rather, the matter is relative to others. And the sun stands forever, for it is not compounded like created beings from the four elements, even though the standing of the sun changes according to the winds." "<b>My judgments</b> — it is known that the judgments of the wisdom of the stars are according to the arrangement of the ministers in their relation to the sun, and there are judgments in the relations that contradict one another, and because of this the practitioners of judgment err. Therefore he said of the judgments of HaShem: they are righteous altogether. And after he finished speaking on the superiority of Torah, which benefits the discerning in the world to come, he mentioned it corresponding to the pleasures of this world."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "Reading יתר as יתיר (permit); the root could also mean 'remove/abolish.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:53.857490713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}